<a name="mysqlclientprotocol"/><h1>Client Protocol Flags</h1>

<p>The <i>clientprotocol</i> option sets which client protocol the MySQL protocol module offers.  It defaults to 41, which is what every currently supported MySQL/MariaDB client expects.  Set it to anything else (eg. 9) only for clients older than MySQL 4.1.  0, or anything that isn't a number, is the same as leaving it out.  It has no effect when <i>handshake</i> is set to 9 (see <a href="mysqlprotohandshake.html">Handshake Protocol Version</a>).</p>

